      ":question/id": "cea05b4d-a2d8-54f8-8de7-af022ab43532",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}9x+18y-81z &=-126 \\\\ x+2y-9z &=-14 \\\\ 3x+6y-27z &=-42\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}9 & 18 & -81 & -126 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -9 & -14 \\\\ 3 & 6 & -27 & -42\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_1\\leftrightarrow R_2\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -9 & -14 \\\\ 9 & 18 & -81 & -126 \\\\ 3 & 6 & -27 & -42\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+(-9)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -9 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 6 & -27 & -42\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_3:=R_3+(-3)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -9 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n",
